# A structure member as the variable a function's VAR_OUTPUT is assigned to.
#
# Derivation: in a formal call, "output => variable" assigns the output to
# the variable after the call (ed.3 6.6.1.7.1 table 20; 6.6.1.3; ed.2
# 2.5.1.1); a member of a structured variable, and a member of an element of
# an array of structures, are variables (ed.3 6.4.4.2, 6.4.4.3, 7.3.1).
# p and pa are the program's VAR, initially 0 (ed.3 table 10) and retained
# between cycles. Integer / truncates toward zero and MOD takes the sign of
# the dividend (table 30); every dividend here is positive.
#   cycle 0, i=1, x=9:  q = 9/4 = 2,  p.y = 1; q2 = 10/4 = 2, pa[1].y = 2  -> e 2 0 0
#   cycle 1, i=3, x=10: q = 10/4 = 2, p.y = 2; q2 = 11/4 = 2, pa[3].y = 3  -> e 2 0 3
#   cycle 2, i=2, x=5:  q = 5/4 = 1,  p.y = 1; q2 = 6/4 = 1,  pa[2].y = 2  -> e 2 2 3
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: i x
outputs: q q2 py e1 e2 e3
status: conformant
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 6.6.1.7.1 (table 20), 6.6.1.3, 6.4.4.2, 7.3.1
---
0 i=1 x=9 => q=2 q2=2 py=1 e1=2 e2=0 e3=0
1 i=3 x=10 => q=2 q2=2 py=2 e1=2 e2=0 e3=3
2 i=2 x=5 => q=1 q2=1 py=1 e1=2 e2=2 e3=3
